<div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text paragraph--view-mode--default paragraph--id--820372">
  <div class="paragraph__column">     
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text-content field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="tex2jax_process"><h2>Remote Sensing</h2><p>Remote sensing is the acquiring of information from a distance. NASA observes Earth and other planetary bodies via remote instruments on space-based platforms (e.g., satellites or spacecraft) and on aircraft that detect and record reflected or emitted energy. Remote instruments, which provide a global perspective and a wealth of data about Earth systems, enable data-informed decision making based on the current and future state of our planet.</p><p>For more information, check out the <a href="/learn/trainings/fundamentals-remote-sensing" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="af64a6d5-57c4-4965-a724-c913100d2a63" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Fundamentals of Remote Sensing">Fundamentals of Remote Sensing training</a> from the Applied Remote Sensing Training (ARSET) program.</p></div></div>
      
  </div>
</div>

      </div>
    
          <div  class="layout__region--second col-12 col-md-4 ps-md-1">
        



