</div></div><div  class="mb-5 _none"><div  class="w-100">  
  <div  class="layout row no-gutters layout-builder__layout">
    
                        <div  class="col-12">
          
<div class="_none mb-7 block-content-interactive_content_panel block block-block-content block-block-content912933fd-d440-42e0-b31c-f23c4bc1a792">
  
    
      <div class="content">

                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
      



<div  data-component-id="wst_component_library:bootstrap-interactive-content-panel" class="bicp-component-wrapper background-dark py-8">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="bicp-header-area row">
              <div class="bicp-component-title col-12 col-md-9 col-lg-8 col-xl-7">
          <h2 class="">Understanding Metadata</h2>
        </div>
                    <div class="bicp-component-description  col-12 col-md-9 col-lg-8 col-xl-7 mt-3">
          This interactive tool helps users navigate and understand essential metadata on our Earth science dataset landing pages. Through guided examples and hands-on exploration, learn critical context about our data to aid you in your own scientific discoveries. 


        </div>
          </div>

    <div class="bicp-content-area mt-6 px-3 px-lg-7 px-md-4 py-7 row">

      <div class="bicp-content-nav col-12 col-md-4 col-lg-3 ps-0 pe-3 mb-4 mb-md-0">

                  <span class="bicp-heading">Interactive</span>
        
                  <h3 class="mt-1">Parts of the Earthdata Dataset Landing Page</h3>
        
                  <div class="bicp-panel-nav mt-3">

                          <span class="panel-items-title">Explore</span>
            
            <ul class="nav flex-column" id="bicp-content-panel-tablist" role="tablist">
              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link active" id="1-long-name-entry-title-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-long-name-entry-title-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-long-name-entry-title-tab-pane" aria-selected="true">
                    Long Name/Entry Title
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This element describes the title of the dataset. Long Name is synonymous with Entry Title.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-short-name-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-short-name-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-short-name-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Short Name
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The Short Name is an abbreviated name for a dataset.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-version-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-version-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-version-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Version
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Version is used to distinguish between versions of a given data<br>product (e.g., produced using different processing algorithms or updates to calibration parameters).<br>It is encouraged to use the latest version of a data product.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-digital-object-identifier-doi-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-digital-object-identifier-doi-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-digital-object-identifier-doi-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Digital Object Identifier (DOI)
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The Digital Object Identifier (DOI) is a persistent identifier that is used to uniquely identify objects including datasets and documents. The DOI field also includes the option to provide information on the authority that registers the DOI, as well as the DOI of the previous version of the record. <a href="/node/47462" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="d231510d-af46-431d-badf-3e1e85d32e2b" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Learn more about DOIs</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-center-project-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-center-project-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-center-project-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Center/Project
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This is the data provider for the data collection.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-cloud-icon-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-cloud-icon-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-cloud-icon-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Cloud Icon
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The cloud icon indicates the dataset lives in the cloud as opposed to on-premises. Clicking on the icon shows the Concept ID for the dataset. <a href="/node/9569" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="55434d9f-7dfb-4d2c-b8d6-43709cfca375" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Learn more about cloud computing</a>.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-data-alert-icon-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-data-alert-icon-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-data-alert-icon-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Data Alert Icon
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>If the dataset has any data alerts (active outage, resolved outage, data update, data release, or retired dataset alert), the alert icon will show. Click on the icon to see the alerts logged.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-copy-url-copy-api-command-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-copy-url-copy-api-command-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-copy-url-copy-api-command-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Copy URL/Copy API Command
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Click on the vertical ellipses for the option to copy the dataset landing page URL, the metadata URL from CMR (copy API command), and there are also a few buttons for sharing the dataset to social media.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-data-format-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-data-format-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-data-format-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Data Format
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>A standard way that information is encoded for storage in a computer file (learn more about <a href="https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/earth-observation-data-basics/data-formats" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="99eeff6a-cf92-49be-a985-b5a9f399feb9" data-entity-substitution="canonical">data formats</a>).</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-dataset-size-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-dataset-size-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-dataset-size-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Dataset Size
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This is a unit of measure for the total collection file size (e.g., KB, MB, TB).</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-spatial-extent-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-spatial-extent-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-spatial-extent-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Spatial Extent
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The Spatial Extent element describes the geographic coverage of the data. At the collection-level, the spatial extent describes the area of the Earth that a data product covers as a whole. For specific files or granules, the spatial extent describes the area covered by that individual file.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-spatial-resolution-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-spatial-resolution-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-spatial-resolution-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Spatial Resolution
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Spatial resolution is the Horizontal Data Resolution which describes the resolution of data that has been georeferenced to a geodetic datum, and&nbsp;is defined as the smallest horizontal distance between successive elements of data in a dataset. <a href="/node/47464" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="6f7a2289-be52-4282-94aa-8471c2dfa73e" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Read more about resolutions and Earth science data</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-temporal-extent-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-temporal-extent-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-temporal-extent-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Temporal Extent
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Temporal Extent describes when data were acquired or collected.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-documents-and-resources-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-documents-and-resources-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-documents-and-resources-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Documents and Resources
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This is where you will find the documents related to the data collection (User Guide, Algorithm Theoretical Basis Document (ATBD)) and learning resources that use the data collection.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-publications-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-publications-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-publications-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Publications
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This is a list of publications that cite the data collection.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-variables-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-variables-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-variables-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Variables
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Variables are a set of physical properties whose values determine the characteristics or behavior of something. For example, temperature and pressure are variables of the atmosphere. Parameters and variables can be used interchangeably. Variable level attributes provide individual information for each variable.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-platforms-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-platforms-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-platforms-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Platforms
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The platform is used to collect the data available in the dataset. <a href="/node/12706" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="110786cf-53b9-44aa-b486-6dd4cbcca6a2" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Explore platforms on Earthdata</a>.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-instruments-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-instruments-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-instruments-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Instruments
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The instrument is used to collect the data available in the dataset. <a href="/node/12718" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="5c23e41f-c27e-418c-b129-daa7711a325a" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Explore instruments on Earthdata</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-coordinate-system-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-coordinate-system-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-coordinate-system-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Coordinate System
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Cartesian and Geodetic are the choices to display for coordinate system in the metadata. Cartesian refers to a grid that helps us pinpoint exactly where something is located. Think of perpendicular axes (x-axis and y-axis in 2-dimensional) that intersect at the origin (0,0) to define locations (coordinates) for points in space. Geodetic coordinates account for the curve of the Earth and typically use latitude (north/south), longitude (east/west), and height above sea level to pinpoint locations.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-granule-spatial-representation-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-granule-spatial-representation-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-granule-spatial-representation-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Granule Spatial Representation
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The same definition as Coordinate System above except on a smaller scale since a granule is one part or chunk of a data collection.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-temporal-resolution-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-temporal-resolution-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-temporal-resolution-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Temporal Resolution
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Temporal resolution&nbsp;is the time it takes for a space-based platform to complete an orbit and revisit the same observation area. Temporal resolution depends on the orbit, the instrument's characteristics, and the swath width. <a href="/node/47464" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="6f7a2289-be52-4282-94aa-8471c2dfa73e" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Read more about resolutions and Earth science data</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-concept-id-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-concept-id-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-concept-id-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Concept ID
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This is another unique identifier for a data collection in the Common Metadata Repository (CMR).</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-data-state-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-data-state-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-data-state-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Data State
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The Collection Progress or Data State describes the production status of the dataset. The Collection Progress element leverages a controlled vocabulary to ensure consistency across data collections. <a href="/node/16545" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="18394e5d-85e1-48d2-9737-fbcaa1a7469b" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Learn more about the Dataset Lifecycle</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-number-of-files-granules-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-number-of-files-granules-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-number-of-files-granules-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Number of Files/Granules
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>This number indicates how many files or granules are in a data collection.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-processing-level-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-processing-level-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-processing-level-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Processing Level
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>An identifier indicating the level at which the data in the collection are processed, ranging from level 0 (raw instrument data at full resolution) to level 4 (model output or analysis results). <a href="/node/9529" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="b8b4052c-240f-4bdd-a6f2-d70bac856761" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Learn more about Data Processing Levels</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-science-keywords-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-science-keywords-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-science-keywords-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Science Keywords
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>Science Keywords are synonymous with Topics and Science Disciplines. Related science keywords are selected by the metadata curator based on the <a href="/node/13526" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="93511641-58ad-4c9d-b7f8-875b537ba77e" data-entity-substitution="canonical">Global Change Master Directory</a> and relate the data collection to potential application areas, resources, and other related information. <a href="/topics/glossary">View all topics on Earthdata</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-citation-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-citation-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-citation-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    Citation
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The citation information is provided for data users to easily cite the data used in their publications.&nbsp;</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

              
                                                
                <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                  <button class="nav-link" id="1-file-naming-convention-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab"
                          data-bs-target="#1-file-naming-convention-tab-pane" type="button" role="tab"
                          aria-controls="1-file-naming-convention-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">
                    File Naming Convention
                  </button>
                                      <div class="bicp-item-description">
                      <p>The File Naming Convention refers to the naming convention of the data set's (Collection's) data files along with a description of the granule file construction.</p>
                    </div>
                                  </li>

                          </ul>

          </div>
              </div>

